```apex
public with sharing class OpportunityPipelineHandler {

    public static void handle(List<Opportunity> newList, Map<Id, Opportunity> oldMap,
                              Boolean isInsert, Boolean isUpdate, Boolean isDelete, Boolean isUndelete) {
        Set<Id> accountIds = new Set<Id>();

        if (isInsert || isUndelete) {
            for (Opportunity o : newList) {
                if (o.AccountId != null) {
                    accountIds.add(o.AccountId);
                }
            }
        } else if (isDelete) {
            for (Opportunity o : oldMap.values()) {
                if (o.AccountId != null) {
                    accountIds.add(o.AccountId);
                }
            }
        } else if (isUpdate) {
            for (Opportunity o : newList) {
                Opportunity old = oldMap.get(o.Id);
                if (o.AccountId != old.AccountId
                    || o.Amount != old.Amount
                    || o.IsClosed != old.IsClosed) {
                    if (o.AccountId != null) {
                        accountIds.add(o.AccountId);
                    }
                    if (old.AccountId != null) {
                        accountIds.add(old.AccountId);
                    }
                }
            }
        }

        if (!accountIds.isEmpty()) {
            recalculate(accountIds);
        }
    }

    private static void recalculate(Set<Id> accountIds) {
        Map<Id, Decimal> sums = new Map<Id, Decimal>();
        Map<Id, Integer> counts = new Map<Id, Integer>();

        for (AggregateResult ar : [
            SELECT AccountId acc, SUM(Amount) total, COUNT(Id) cnt
            FROM Opportunity
            WHERE AccountId IN :accountIds AND IsClosed = false
            GROUP BY AccountId
        ]) {
            Id accId = (Id) ar.get('acc');
            Decimal total = (Decimal) ar.get('total');
            sums.put(accId, total == null ? 0 : total);
            counts.put(accId, (Integer) ar.get('cnt'));
        }

        List<Account> toUpdate = new List<Account>();
        for (Account a : [
            SELECT Id, FB_Open_Pipeline__c, FB_Open_Opportunities__c
            FROM Account WHERE Id IN :accountIds
        ]) {
            Decimal newSum = sums.containsKey(a.Id) ? sums.get(a.Id) : 0;
            Decimal newCnt = counts.containsKey(a.Id) ? counts.get(a.Id) : 0;
            Decimal curSum = a.FB_Open_Pipeline__c;
            Decimal curCnt = a.FB_Open_Opportunities__c;
            if (curSum == null || curCnt == null || curSum != newSum || curCnt != newCnt) {
                toUpdate.add(new Account(
                    Id = a.Id,
                    FB_Open_Pipeline__c = newSum,
                    FB_Open_Opportunities__c = newCnt
                ));
            }
        }

        if (!toUpdate.isEmpty()) {
            update toUpdate;
        }
    }
}
```

Design notes:

- `Level__c` can be blank, so a filter like `Level__c != 'ERROR'` would be unsafe. In SOQL, `!=` does not match nulls the way you might expect in some contexts, so I handle blanks explicitly with `Level__c = null OR Level__c != 'ERROR'`.
- Case: SOQL string comparison is case-insensitive, so `'error'` also matches `ERROR`, which is acceptable.
- Volume: a single run could hit the DML row limit of 10,000, so the schedulable should hand off to Batch Apex. I implemented `Database.Batchable` in the same class, with the schedulable's `execute` calling `Database.executeBatch`. A QueryLocator handles up to 50 million rows.
- Security: the purge is a system job, so it runs in system mode. I use `with sharing` as the default, but a purge job must see all records. I use `without sharing` deliberately so the purge is not limited by the running user's record visibility. Deletion of the records is intended.
- Cutoffs: they are computed as datetimes in the batch's `start`, using `System.now().addDays(-30)` and `addDays(-180)`. The condition is "created more than 30 days ago," so `CreatedDate < cutoff`.
- Scheduling: the cron expression for 02:00 daily is `0 0 2 * * ?`. `System.schedule` returns the Id.

