Design notes:
- The component keeps an internal `_value` (set by the parent through the `value` setter) and an `_activeValue`. When the parent sets `value`, the active option moves to it.
- Option ids must be unique and stable. I generate them from the index (`opt-0`, `opt-1`, ...). LWC rewrites ids to make them unique per component instance, and `aria-activedescendant` on a static template attribute can break across ids. I'm using the same-template reference, which LWC handles correctly because both the `id` and the `aria-activedescendant` are in one template.
- The active option is tracked by value, with an index fallback. If the active value is no longer in the options (options changed), it falls back to the selected option, then to the first option.
- `data-value` is set from the option value.
- Clicks use `event.currentTarget.dataset.value`. Values may not be strings, so I look up by index (`data-index`) instead and read the real value from the options array.
- Clicking the already-selected option still makes it active but dispatches nothing.

