NPSP's standard mechanism (the Affiliations trigger, `AFFL_Affiliations_TDTM`) handles two things:

- When an affiliation is inserted with Primary = true, it sets `Contact.npsp__Primary_Affiliation__c` to the organization.
- When `Contact.npsp__Primary_Affiliation__c` changes, it marks the old primary affiliation as Former, non-primary, with an end date of today.

I therefore insert only the new affiliations and never touch the Contact lookup myself, because setting it directly can interfere with the trigger and risks changing the household account.

Design:
- Query 1: the contacts' existing affiliations (`npe5__Contact__c IN :contactIds`, `npe5__Primary__c = true`, `npe5__Status__c = 'Current'`). This tells me which contacts already have the organization as their primary affiliation, so I skip them.
- Query 2: `Contact.npsp__Primary_Affiliation__c`, because the lookup can be set without an affiliation record. A contact whose lookup already equals the organization, and who has a primary affiliation to it, is skipped. Where the lookup matches but no affiliation exists, I insert one.
- DML 1: insert the new affiliations. When NPSP processes an insert with Primary = true, it updates the contact's lookup and former-izes the previous primary affiliation.

An existing non-primary affiliation (for example Former) between the contact and the organization could be reused, but this would need a third query. To stay within 2 queries I query all of the contact's affiliations for the target contacts in a single query, which covers both cases: the primary one, and an existing one for the same organization. If an existing affiliation to the same organization exists but isn't primary or current, I update it to Current and primary, with the end date cleared, instead of inserting a duplicate. That is the second DML. I do the update and the insert in separate DML statements, which is within the 2 DML limit.

The contact lookup check also uses the first query, which selects the contact's affiliations with the parent lookup field in the same query. That is not needed, so I leave it out. I skip a contact only when a Current primary affiliation to the organization exists.

```apex
public with sharing class EmployerService {

    public static void setCurrentEmployers(Map<Id, Id> employerByContactId) {
        if (employerByContactId == null || employerByContactId.isEmpty()) {
            return;
        }

        Map<Id, Id> wanted = new Map<Id, Id>();
        for (Id contactId : employerByContactId.keySet()) {
            Id orgId = employerByContactId.get(contactId);
            if (contactId != null && orgId != null) {
                wanted.put(contactId, orgId);
            }
        }
        if (wanted.isEmpty()) {
            return;
        }

        // Single query: all affiliations for the contacts involved
        Map<Id, Map<Id, npe5__Affiliation__c>> existing =
            new Map<Id, Map<Id, npe5__Affiliation__c>>();
        for (npe5__Affiliation__c a : [
            SELECT Id, npe5__Contact__c, npe5__Organization__c, npe5__Status__c,
                   npe5__Primary__c, npe5__EndDate__c
            FROM npe5__Affiliation__c
            WHERE npe5__Contact__c IN :wanted.keySet()
            WITH USER_MODE
            ORDER BY CreatedDate DESC
        ]) {
            Map<Id, npe5__Affiliation__c> byOrg = existing.get(a.npe5__Contact__c);
            if (byOrg == null) {
                byOrg = new Map<Id, npe5__Affiliation__c>();
                existing.put(a.npe5__Contact__c, byOrg);
            }
            // keep the first (most recent) per organization,
            // but prefer one that is already current and primary
            npe5__Affiliation__c prior = byOrg.get(a.npe5__Organization__c);
            if (prior == null
                || (!(prior.npe5__Primary__c && prior.npe5__Status__c == 'Current')
                    && a.npe5__Primary__c && a.npe5__Status__c == 'Current')) {
                byOrg.put(a.npe5__Organization__c, a);
            }
        }

        List<npe5__Affiliation__c> toInsert = new List<npe5__Affiliation__c>();
        List<npe5__Affiliation__c> toUpdate = new List<npe5__Affiliation__c>();

        for (Id contactId : wanted.keySet()) {
            Id orgId = wanted.get(contactId);
            npe5__Affiliation__c match = existing.containsKey(contactId)
                ? existing.get(contactId).get(orgId) : null;

            if (match == null) {
                toInsert.add(new npe5__Affiliation__c(
                    npe5__Contact__c = contactId,
                    npe5__Organization__c = orgId,
                    npe5__Status__c = 'Current',
                    npe5__Primary__c = true,
                    npe5__StartDate__c = Date.today()
                ));
            } else if (match.npe5__Primary__c && match.npe5__Status__c == 'Current') {
                continue; // already the current primary employer
            } else {
                match.npe5__Status__c = 'Current';
                match.npe5__Primary__c = true;
                match.npe5__EndDate__c = null;
                toUpdate.add(match);
            }
        }

        // NPSP's affiliation trigger sets Contact.npsp__Primary_Affiliation__c
        // and ends the previous primary affiliation.
        if (!toUpdate.isEmpty()) {
            update as user toUpdate;
        }
        if (!toInsert.isEmpty()) {
            insert as user toInsert;
        }
    }
}
