I'm using NPSP's BDI Apex API, `npsp.BDI_DataImport_API.processDataImportRecords(diSettings, diRecords, isDryRun)`. It processes the records synchronously and writes results back to the Data Import records. Per NPSP docs, the signature is:

`public static Id processDataImportRecords(npsp__Data_Import_Settings__c diSettings, List<npsp__DataImport__c> dataImports, Boolean isDryRun)`

The `npsp__Data_Import_Settings__c` record comes from `npsp.BDI_DataImport_API.getDefaultDataImportSettings()`, which returns the org's settings. The API processes the records passed in, and the caller must insert them first so they have Ids. After processing I re-query the records to read the result fields.

Design choices:
- Insert the Data Import records with `Database.insert(records, false)`. A row that fails to insert gets an error result, and only the successfully inserted rows go to BDI.
- Set `npsp__Donation_Donor__c = 'Contact1'`.
- Do not delete the Data Import records, since they serve as the audit trail.
- Chunk processing: BDI is designed for batches. For 200 records the API is fine in one call, since NPSP's own batch size default is 50 but synchronous processing of 200 is the documented use case for the API. I'll pass the whole list in one call.
- Results map back to inputs by index. I keep a list of the inserted records aligned with the input, then re-query by Id to get the status fields.
- Null gift entries are returned as failures rather than throwing.
- `success` is true when `npsp__Status__c == 'Imported'`. The contact comes from `npsp__Contact1Imported__c` and the opportunity from `npsp__DonationImported__c`.
- If BDI throws, I catch the exception and mark all rows that were staged as failed with the message.

```apex
public with sharing class GiftImportService {

    public class WebGift {
        public String firstName;
        public String lastName;
        public String email;
        public Decimal amount;
        public Date giftDate;
    }

    public class ImportResult {
        public Boolean success;
        public Id contactId;
        public Id opportunityId;
        public String errorMessage;
    }

    public static List<ImportResult> importGifts(List<WebGift> gifts) {
        List<ImportResult> results = new List<ImportResult>();
        if (gifts == null || gifts.isEmpty()) {
            return results;
        }

        List<npsp__DataImport__c> staged = new List<npsp__DataImport__c>();
        List<Integer> stagedIndex = new List<Integer>();

        for (Integer i = 0; i < gifts.size(); i++) {
            WebGift g = gifts[i];
            ImportResult r = new ImportResult();
            r.success = false;
            results.add(r);
            if (g == null) {
                r.errorMessage = 'Gift is missing.';
                continue;
            }
            npsp__DataImport__c di = new npsp__DataImport__c();
            di.npsp__Contact1_Firstname__c = g.firstName;
            di.npsp__Contact1_Lastname__c = g.lastName;
            di.npsp__Contact1_Personal_Email__c = g.email;
            di.npsp__Donation_Amount__c = g.amount;
            di.npsp__Donation_Date__c = g.giftDate;
            di.npsp__Donation_Donor__c = 'Contact1';
            staged.add(di);
            stagedIndex.add(i);
        }

        if (staged.isEmpty()) {
            return results;
        }

        List<Database.SaveResult> saves = Database.insert(staged, false);
        List<npsp__DataImport__c> toProcess = new List<npsp__DataImport__c>();
        Map<Id, Integer> idToIndex = new Map<Id, Integer>();
        for (Integer j = 0; j < saves.size(); j++) {
            Integer idx = stagedIndex[j];
            if (saves[j].isSuccess()) {
                toProcess.add(staged[j]);
                idToIndex.put(staged[j].Id, idx);
            } else {
                results[idx].errorMessage = saves[j].getErrors()[0].getMessage();
            }
        }

        if (toProcess.isEmpty()) {
            return results;
        }

        String processError;
        try {
            npsp__Data_Import_Settings__c diSettings =
                npsp.BDI_DataImport_API.getDefaultDataImportSettings();
            npsp.BDI_DataImport_API.processDataImportRecords(diSettings, toProcess, false);
        } catch (Exception e) {
            processError = e.getMessage();
        }

        List<npsp__DataImport__c> processed = [
            SELECT Id, npsp__Status__c, npsp__Contact1Imported__c,
                   npsp__DonationImported__c, npsp__FailureInformation__c
            FROM npsp__DataImport__c
            WHERE Id IN :idToIndex.keySet()
        ];

        for (npsp__DataImport__c di : processed) {
            ImportResult r = results[idToIndex.get(di.Id)];
            if (di.npsp__Status__c == 'Imported') {
                r.success = true;
                r.contactId = di.npsp__Contact1Imported__c;
                r.opportunityId = di.npsp__DonationImported__c;
            } else {
                r.success = false;
                r.contactId = di.npsp__Contact1Imported__c;
