```apex
global with sharing class OPP_MajorGiftFollowUp_TDTM extends npsp.TDTM_Runnable {

    private static final Decimal MAJOR_GIFT_THRESHOLD = 5000;
    private static final String TASK_SUBJECT = 'Major gift thank-you call';

    global override npsp.TDTM_Runnable.DmlWrapper run(
        List<SObject> newlist,
        List<SObject> oldlist,
        npsp.TDTM_Runnable.Action triggerAction,
        Schema.DescribeSObjectResult objResult
    ) {
        npsp.TDTM_Runnable.DmlWrapper dmlWrapper = new npsp.TDTM_Runnable.DmlWrapper();

        if (newlist == null || newlist.isEmpty()) {
            return dmlWrapper;
        }

        Boolean isInsert = triggerAction == npsp.TDTM_Runnable.Action.AfterInsert;
        Boolean isUpdate = triggerAction == npsp.TDTM_Runnable.Action.AfterUpdate;
        if (!isInsert && !isUpdate) {
            return dmlWrapper;
        }

        Map<Id, Opportunity> oldMap = new Map<Id, Opportunity>();
        if (isUpdate && oldlist != null) {
            for (SObject so : oldlist) {
                Opportunity o = (Opportunity) so;
                oldMap.put(o.Id, o);
            }
        }

        for (SObject so : newlist) {
            Opportunity opp = (Opportunity) so;

            if (!qualifies(opp)) {
                continue;
            }

            if (isUpdate) {
                Opportunity oldOpp = oldMap.get(opp.Id);
                if (oldOpp != null && qualifies(oldOpp)) {
                    continue;
                }
            }

            if (opp.CloseDate == null) {
                continue;
            }

            Task t = new Task(
                Subject = TASK_SUBJECT,
                Priority = 'High',
                Status = 'Not Started',
                WhatId = opp.Id,
                WhoId = (Id) opp.get('npsp__Primary_Contact__c'),
                OwnerId = opp.OwnerId,
                ActivityDate = opp.CloseDate.addDays(3)
            );
            dmlWrapper.objectsToInsert.add(t);
        }

        return dmlWrapper;
    }

    private static Boolean qualifies(Opportunity opp) {
        return opp.IsWon == true
            && opp.Amount != null
            && opp.Amount >= MAJOR_GIFT_THRESHOLD;
    }
}
```

Two changes are needed in the `fsl-dispatch` package directory:

1. **Pin the dependency to the promoted build.** `2.3.0.LATEST` resolves to the latest build, which could be beta build 8. Using the `fsl-scheduling@2.3.0-6` alias pins it to build 6. The dependency entry takes either `versionNumber` with a build number or an alias. With an alias, you drop `versionNumber` and write `"package": "fsl-scheduling@2.3.0-6"`. A `versionNumber` of `2.3.0.6` is not supported for dependencies, because a specific build is referenced by alias. `LATEST` can also be combined with `--released-only`, but that is a command-line flag and not a file change. The alias is the file-based way, so I used it.

2. **Stop build numbers being reused.** The `versionNumber` of `1.8.0.3` is the last created build, so creating a version again would reuse 3 (or fail). Changing it to `1.8.0.NEXT` makes each creation auto-increment to build 4 and beyond.

Nothing else changes, including the scheduling package's own `2.4.0.NEXT` and the aliases.

